  "lineage": "Afro-descendant ritual and festive repertoire of Colombia's Pacific littoral (Chocó, Cauca, Nariño) and Atlantic coast, documented from the 1960s by Delia Zapata Olivella and later by Petronio Álvarez festival ensembles, built on marimba de chonta ostinati, cununo and bombo cross-rhythms, guasá shakers and interlocked female chorus over currulao's 6/8 and bullerengue's hand-drum 2/4.",
